  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 4a2b061e491659d4e8424ca22aacc1c7, type: 3}
  m_Name: Read_ZoneProfile_Fabrication_Early
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::Hecton8.World.WorldExpeditionLoopProfile
  profileId: loop.profile.fabrication.early
  profileLabel: Fabrication Early Read
  entryBeat: A visible outpost or fabrication stop reads as a reliable human foothold.
  routineBeat: The player quickly understands this is a place to reset, craft, and
    reassess.
  reliefBeat: This area acts as a dependable pressure break before or after riskier
    water.
  pressureBeat: Pressure lives mostly outside the stop, not inside it.
  payoffBeat: The reward is readiness for the next self-chosen trip, not a scripted
    loot moment.
  exitBeat: Departure should feel deliberate and clean, not funnelled.
  playerFreedomRule: The player decides whether this stop matters now, later, or
    not at all.
  softProgressionPull: The place quietly advertises preparation and optional regrouping.
  optionalDetourRule: Even a brief glance should make the outpost memorable as a
    future reset point.
  returnLogic: Repeat visits should feel smart and self-directed, never mandatory.
  masteryLogic: Experienced players use the stop as a flexible logistics anchor between
    different plans.
  playerPromise: A stable pocket of control inside a wider uncertain world.
  routeMemoryRule: Memory should come from the outpost silhouette and its relation
    to nearby risk water.
  failureMode: If the stop is slow, noisy, or unclear, it stops working as a relief
    space.
